| Goal | Mechanism |
|---|---|
| **Encryption at rest** | Every value is encrypted with **AES-256-GCM** under a key derived from the master password via **PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-256** (100 000 iterations, random 128-bit salt). The stored bytes are `IV ∥ ciphertext+tag`, so a reader learns only the approximate plaintext length. |
| **Owner isolation** | Each secret is stored under a **length-prefixed key** `secret:<ownerLen>:<owner>:<nameLen>:<name>`, which is collision-free even when owner/name contain `:`, `/`, `|`, spaces, or newlines. `list` prefix-filters on the owner portion. |
| **Tamper detection (including cross-secret copy)** | The **AES-GCM additional authenticated data (AAD)** is the UTF-8 encoding of the full storage key. Copying one secret's blob to another owner/name changes the AAD used at decryption time, so the GCM authentication tag won't verify and `get` throws. Any bit-flip in the stored bytes is likewise caught by the tag. |
| **Wrong master password** | A verification canary (known plaintext encrypted with the derived key and a fixed AAD) is stored in `__secret_store_meta__`. At `createSecretStore` time the canary is decrypted; a wrong password produces a different key and the decryption rejects, so the constructor throws before any store is handed back. |

